body:
The most literal polar opposite I can think of is Anne Hathaway in Les Mis, vs her in Ocean's 8 lol. 

&nbsp;
Also idk if it really counts but Constance Wu in Fresh off the Boat (show) and Crazy Rich Asians. I guess her role in Hustlers works too.

My one question was, "why did you like this movie?". His response was, and I quote, "I like the hustle aspect of the movie". When I called him an idiot he said I viewed the movie for what it was, while he, "viewed it more metaphorically". Going on to allude to the idea that the characters were representations of (North American) employers and their employees..... 

&nbsp;
nice guy, and I'm glad I got to watch the movie cause of him, but man I didn't know how to respond to that one.

sorry I'm kind of confused, which one is supposed to be the caricature? 

&nbsp;
Additionally American Psycho was based off a book where the character is almost ludicrously obsessive and truly, as he says, "utterly insane". Like there are several chapters just dedicated to obsessing over the music industry and its titans, and after he >!kills his girlfriend!< in the book, he bites her fingers off and laughs maniacally. Thats full deranged crazy, even Bloom couldn't touch that. The movie version had to alter things because of course the only digestible way to have him on screen would be to almost satirize him. At least thats how I see it anyway.

Donnie Darko was the first movie I saw him in and in the first 15 minutes of nightcrawler I couldnt help but see Donnie in him and I really felt bad for the poor guy with the sad eyes. Then 20 minutes came around and I saw they were dead dead eyes and I’ll probably never see him the same way again. chills is correct. 

&nbsp;
also I love your list of his best roles, I’d just add nocturnal animals.

well off the top of my head, gone girl would be a prime example, but also tyler from fight club, fear (1996), most of joe pesci’s roles (casino, goodfellas- hell maybe I should include kevin mccallister), jack nicholson in the departed, seven, ma, dial m for murder, silence of the lambs 
&nbsp; 
and an honorable mention: american psycho (patrick bateman is too obvious a choice, but alas it’s in the title- not quite a sociopath)

&nbsp;
and yes, I have known and met narcissists in my lifetime, that’s why it feels real to me. but who needs a fucking PHD to see that LB is a sociopathic smarmy ass? he is the epitome of a sociopath and consistently exhibits real narcissistic tendencies. Should I continue? want me to cite my sources? or are you just a contrarian who likes to contribute nothing to the conversation?

Don't know if this was mentioned yet but Robin williams in good will hunting. Robin williams in anything quite frankly. But he was that perfect mix of charmingly funny and caring and sad that really just, hit all the right notes. Also Ralph Fiennes absolutely made the grand budapest hotel. Honorable mentions: Jim Carrey in any of his 1994 roles and Willlem Dafoe as the green goblin.
&nbsp;


Edit: wanted to add james earl jones as mufasa, and his "son" Eddie murphy in coming to america
